hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20974","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: I heard an elder from Qays narrating from his father that he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us, and with us was a difficult young she-camel none could handle. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, approached it and wiped its udder, so it filled and he milked. He said: When my father died, I came having tied him in his shroud, and I took palm-fibre and tied the shroud with it, and he said: Do not torment your father with sulla, Hammad said it three times. He said: Then he uncovered his chest and cast away the sulla, then spat upon his chest until I saw the specks of his spit upon his chest."
